    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d932">

                <pb facs="0828" n="816" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg816"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/19096: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kelley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-01-30T17:00:00+02:00">January 30, 1942—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:03 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>58. I have been informed by a person in confidence of President that latter was
                    very much pleased with Ambassador MacMurray’s interview in Baltimore <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Sun</hi> and considers it an excellent expose of
                    Turkey’s position.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kelley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
